  "articleBody": "Feeling frustrated because your business isn't getting cited by AI Overviews, ChatGPT, or other answer engines? It's a common challenge, especially with how quickly the digital landscape is changing. Traditional SEO focused on keywords for those '10 blue links,' but AI works differently, prioritizing content that directly answers questions and relies heavily on structured data. Many local businesses find their existing websites, often built on heavy CMS themes like WordPress or Wix, just aren't designed for AI crawlers. These platforms can slow down or even prevent AI bots from properly understanding your content. Plus, if your FAQs are thin or outdated, or you're not specifically targeting the real questions people ask online, AI systems won't have the rich, structured information they need to recommend you.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice\n\nYour existing website's structure and age play a big role here. If your site is heavily reliant on JavaScript or has a lot of 'render-blocking' elements, AI crawlers might struggle. The type of content you have is also key; AI systems look for clear, fact-dense answers, not just broad keyword mentions. Businesses operating in super competitive local markets often face an uphill battle too, as directories and aggregators tend to dominate AI answers.\n\nMany businesses also overlook the importance of systematically targeting those real questions people ask on platforms like Quora, Reddit, or even Google Business Profile Q&A. AI Visibility Solutions focuses on researching these exact questions, creating an 'AI Resource Library' of schema-dense, static HTML pages designed explicitly for machine consumption. This includes generating concise, direct-answer paragraphs that are optimized for AI extraction, ensuring your content is fact-dense and semantically relevant.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n\nIf you're noticing your competitors getting cited and you're not, or if your current website isn't built with AI ingestion in mind, it's probably time to get some professional help. This is especially true for brand new businesses or those with little domain authority on their own site. We help you qualify to be the answer when prospects ask conversational questions online, whether in Google or AI search, by building an AI-ready knowledge base.\n\nReady to get your business cited by AI? Let's chat about how an AI Resource Library can put your answers front and center.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-30"
}